# Coverage config (Person 3 / Stage 3).
#
# What is measured
# ----------------
# The Stage 3 crypto core — canonical, merkle, bundle, stage2_adapter,
# stage2_bridge, verify, verify_cli — is unit-covered by tests/test_*.py, as
# is anchor.py: its three refusal paths (no bundle, recomputed root != stored
# root, ABSTAIN verdict) run entirely before any network call and are pinned
# in tests/test_audit_fixes.py.  Those refusals are the highest-value tests in
# the repo and they are counted here.
#
# What is omitted, and why
# ------------------------
#   chain.py   Web3 provider wiring, signing and contract calls.
#   run.py     the argparse CLI / demo driver + `forge` subprocess shims.
#
# An earlier version of this file claimed these had "no unit-testable logic of
# their own".  That was not true and the claim is withdrawn: the pure parts of
# chain.py — to_bytes32, chain_name, rpc_url, registry_address, private_key —
# are now unit-tested in tests/test_chain_units.py, and run.py's command
# surface in tests/test_run.py.  What remains omitted is the part that only a
# node can exercise: building, signing and broadcasting a transaction, and
# shelling out to forge.
#
# Those paths are not untested either — tests/test_chain.py drives them
# against a live Anvil node and the `chain-integration` CI job now fails if
# that file skips.  They are omitted from this percentage only because the
# mocked job cannot reach them, not because nobody checks them.
[run]
omit =
    faceproof/chain.py
    faceproof/run.py
    faceproof/__main__.py

[report]
exclude_also =
    if TYPE_CHECKING:
    raise NotImplementedError
    if __name__ == .__main__.:
